SCOPE — WHAT THIS LICENSE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER

The MIT terms above cover the *software* in this repository: source code,
configuration, build tooling and documentation.

They do NOT cover the datasets and model artefacts, which are licensed
separately:

  * The AegisAI Fraud Corpus (AIFC) and any other corpus produced under
    docs/DATASETS.md is released under CC-BY-4.0, with a documented exclusion
    list for third-party items whose own licence forbids redistribution.
    See docs/DATASETS.md §7.

  * Individual corpus items carry their own `license` field and provenance
    record. An item sourced from a third party keeps that third party's terms;
    this file does not relicense it.

  * Trained model checkpoints under ml/artifacts/ inherit any restrictions of
    the base models they were fine-tuned from. MuRIL is Apache-2.0; check the
    manifest recorded by ml/evaluation/manifest.py before redistributing a
    checkpoint.

This split is deliberate and predates the file. It is written down here because
a bare MIT license at the root of a repository is normally read as covering
everything in it, which would have silently contradicted the CC-BY-4.0 commitment
in docs/DATASETS.md.
